This directory (`vendor/venus-protocol/`) vendors generated and third-party header files under TWO
separate, both permissive, licenses. Which license applies to which file is stated in an
`SPDX-License-Identifier` comment at the top of that file itself — this file exists so the
attribution is unmistakable at the directory level too, not to override anything any individual
header says.

# 1. MIT — Mesa's own generated `venus-protocol` headers

Every `vn_protocol_renderer_*.h` file (the generated Venus protocol decoders this crate's `shim.c`
drives — see `../README`-equivalent docs in `../csrc/shim.c` and the crate's own `src/lib.rs`) is
MIT-licensed, copyright Google LLC (2020, 2022) and Collabora Ltd. (2022) — see each file's own
header comment for its specific copyright line.

