# 2. Apache-2.0 — the Khronos Vulkan headers these decoders build against

`vulkan.h`, `vulkan_core.h`, `vk_platform.h`, and every header under `vk_video/` are Khronos Group's
own Vulkan headers (pulled in because the generated decoders speak in `Vk*` types), copyright
2014-2025 / 2015-2025 The Khronos Group Inc., licensed Apache-2.0 — **not** MIT. Do not assume
everything under `vendor/venus-protocol/` shares one license; these files are the exception, and
their own `SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0` header says so.

The full Apache License, Version 2.0 text is available at
<https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0> and is not reproduced in full here; per its own terms
(§4), redistributing these files under Apache-2.0 requires only that recipients be given a copy of
the License (that URL) and that any changed files be marked as changed — this project has not
modified any of these headers (see `MESA_VERSION`'s "do not modify" rule).

# Why both matter to this crate

`rayland-venus-proto` is LGPL-3.0-or-later (see its own `Cargo.toml`). Both MIT and Apache-2.0 are
permissive and compatible with linking into an LGPL crate; nothing here restricts how this crate may
be built, used or distributed. This file exists purely so a reader — or a future license audit — does
not have to grep every one of the 52 vendored headers to learn that two different upstream projects,
under two different licenses, are represented in this one directory.
